  grh-ln "      <h3><span class='ep' data-pure='Conjugate-Power Phase Averaging &amp; Positive-Series Real-Singularity Trap' data-wb='Alp&ouml;ge &sect;I.10 Dirichlet Character-Twist Positivity &amp; Landau Real-Singularity Lemma'>Conjugate-Power Phase Averaging &amp; Positive-Series Real-Singularity Trap</span></h3>" (
  grh-ln "      <p>By the <span class='ep' data-pure='non-negative series real-boundary singularity principle' data-wb='Landau real-singularity lemma'>non-negative series real-boundary singularity principle</span>, if <span class='m'><i>F</i>(<i>s</i>) = &sum; <i>c</i><sub><i>n</i></sub><i>n</i><sup>&minus;<i>s</i></sup></span> has <span class='m'><i>c</i><sub><i>n</i></sub> &ge; 0</span>, then <span class='m'>|<i>F</i>(&sigma; + <i>it</i>)| &le; <i>F</i>(&sigma;)</span>, so convergence cannot extend past a singularity on <span class='m'>&Re;(<i>s</i>) = &sigma;<sub>0</sub></span> without already diverging at the real point <span class='m'><i>s</i> = &sigma;<sub>0</sub></span>.</p>" (
  grh-ln "      <p>For a complex character <span class='m'>&psi;</span> of order <span class='m'><i>o</i> &ge; 2</span>, raw prime-power terms <span class='m'>&Lambda;(<i>n</i>)&psi;(<i>n</i>)</span> carry complex phases that could cancel. Forming the <span class='ep' data-pure='conjugate-power average' data-wb='Alp&ouml;ge &sect;I.10 twisted combination'>conjugate-power average</span> <span class='m'><i>G</i> + (3<i>o</i>+1)<sup>&minus;1</sup>&sum;<sub><i>j</i>=1</sub><sup><i>o</i>&minus;1</sup> &Re;(<i>G</i><sub>&psi;<sup><i>j</i></sup></sub>)</span> uses <span class='m'>&Re;(&psi;<sup><i>j</i></sup>(<i>n</i>)) &ge; &minus;1</span> to keep every prime-power coefficient strictly above <span class='m'>1/2</span>, preventing phase cancellation from hiding an off-axis zero <span class='m'>&Re;(&rho;) &gt; 1/2</span>.</p>" (
  grh-ln "      <div class='eq'><i>W</i><sub>min</sub>(<i>o</i>) = 1 &minus; (<i>o</i> &minus; 1)/(3<i>o</i> + 1) = (2<i>o</i> + 2)/(3<i>o</i> + 1) &gt; 1/2 &gt; 0 &emsp; (&forall; <i>o</i> &ge; 2)</div>" (
