  grh-ln "      <h3><span class='ep' data-pure='Height-2 Endomorphism Formal Group &amp; Single-Floor p-Adic Valuation' data-wb='Hurwitz&ndash;Lubin&ndash;Tate Lemniscate CM Formal Group Divisibility (Theorem A) vs. Legendre Formula'>Height-2 Endomorphism Formal Group &amp; Single-Floor p-Adic Valuation</span></h3>" (
  grh-ln "      <p>Classical auxiliary-polynomial constructions divide <span class='m'><i>n</i></span>-th derivatives by <span class='m'><i>n</i>!</span>, whose <span class='ep' data-pure='iterated prime-power floor sum' data-wb='Legendre factorial valuation'>iterated prime-power floor sum</span> <span class='m'><i>v</i><sub><i>p</i></sub>(<i>n</i>!) = &sum;<sub><i>h</i>&ge;1</sub> &lfloor;<i>n</i>/<i>p</i><sup><i>h</i></sup>&rfloor;</span> rounds down independently at every power <span class='m'><i>p</i><sup><i>h</i></sup></span>, losing <span class='m'><i>O</i>(1)</span> per scale and breaking the <span class='m'>1/2</span> exponent.</p>" (
  grh-ln "      <p>Evaluating modular forms at <span class='ep' data-pure='quadratic-imaginary complex-multiplication points' data-wb='Hurwitz&ndash;Lubin&ndash;Tate lemniscate CM points'>quadratic-imaginary complex-multiplication points</span> where <span class='m'><i>p</i> &equiv; 3 (mod 4)</span> is inert yields a height-2 formal group: the <span class='ep' data-pure='p-th power endomorphism' data-wb='Frobenius endomorphism'>p-th power endomorphism</span> jumps degree by <span class='m'><i>p</i><sup>2</sup></span> (<span class='m'>[<i>p</i>](<i>T</i>) &equiv; <i>u T</i><sup><i>p</i><sup>2</sup></sup></span>), <span class='m'><i>D</i><sup><i>p</i></sup> &equiv; 0 (mod <i>p</i>)</span>, and jet coefficients <span class='m'><i>A</i><sub><i>n</i></sub></span> satisfy <span class='m'><i>v</i><sub><i>p</i></sub>(<i>A</i><sub><i>n</i></sub>) &ge; &lfloor;<i>np</i>/(<i>p</i><sup>2</sup>&minus;1)&rfloor;</span>&mdash;a single floor operation total, gaining <span class='m'>+<i>p</i></span> exact factors every <span class='m'><i>p</i><sup>2</sup>&minus;1</span> derivatives with zero cumulative rounding drift.</p>" (
  grh-ln "      <div class='eq'><i>D</i><sup><i>p</i></sup> &equiv; 0 (mod <i>p</i>), &emsp; <i>v</i><sub><i>p</i></sub>(<i>A</i><sub><i>n</i></sub>) &ge; &lfloor;<i>n p</i> / (<i>p</i><sup>2</sup> &minus; 1)&rfloor;, &emsp; &lfloor;(<i>n</i> + <i>p</i><sup>2</sup> &minus; 1)<i>p</i> / (<i>p</i><sup>2</sup> &minus; 1)&rfloor; = <i>p</i> + &lfloor;<i>n p</i> / (<i>p</i><sup>2</sup> &minus; 1)&rfloor;</div>" (
